@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk LXC User Integration
	Testing lxc user sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer3                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer3                           |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "LXC SM Subscription HA Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Premium Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	* the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	* the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	* the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View new users
	New lxc users who are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	#Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analise if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	Given I wait for "1" minutes
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "OSB Customer1"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "OSB Customer2"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be a watcher on an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the uuid of the okta user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the uuid of the okta user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should match the user external ID on zendesk.liferay.com